language 0.1.0
module api
  means
    Programmatic interaction between systems and components through explicitly
    published contracts for invoking operations.

entity interface : thing
  means
    interface: a named contract gathering the operations available to an
    external consumer.

entity operation : thing
  means
    operation: an invocable action with definite inputs, results and
    conditions of performance.

entity endpoint : thing
  means
    endpoint: an addressable place through which a consumer reaches an
    interface.

entity request : thing
  means
    request: a transmitted representation of the intent to invoke an
    operation, together with its input data.

entity response : thing
  means
    response: a transmitted representation of the result of invoking an
    operation.

entity parameter : thing
  means
    parameter: a named part of the input or configuration of an operation,
    having a definite type.

entity protocol : thing
  means
    protocol: a set of rules for exchanging messages between parties to an
    interaction.

entity status : thing
  means
    status: a classified outcome of processing a request, conveyed to the
    consumer.

entity error : thing
  means
    error: an unsuccessful outcome of an operation, described by the contract.
